[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5378943762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122696#issuecomment-5378943762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122696","id":5378943762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQJwrEg","user":{"login":"CodeForBeauty","id":121430182,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzzgpg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121430182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeForBeauty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeForBeauty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-22T07:09:57Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T07:09:57Z","body":"Normal matrix multiplication doesn't work well with negative scale.\r\n\r\nThe simplest example is:\r\n\r\nLet's say we have a single triangle that lays on XY plane. It's normals are pointing at +Z. If we scale it by -1 on X axis the normals don't change at all. And vertices get from CCW order into CW which causes the fragment shader later on to incorrectly invert normals.\r\n\r\nHope this makes sense.\r\n\r\nRegarding adding a flag, I just assumed the first bits where in use for something so decided to not touch them.\r\n\r\nI would need the same flag. Is it ok if I just copy paste the common parts from #122150 ?","au